Chapter: ValidationRules
  cites UI chapter Validation

 The character-class rules are the ones to watch, because a character
 class is where an ASCII assumption hides. CCE orders letters by English
 frequency: the digits are code points 3 to 12, lowercase runs 13 to 38,
 uppercase 39 to 64, punctuation 65 to 96, and then sixteen accented Latin
 letters and fifteen Cyrillic ones at 97 to 127.

 We say:

Section: Reporting

  verdict : ValidationResult -> Text
  verdict (r) = if vr-is-ok r then "ok" else "ERR"

  check : ValidationRule, Text -> Text
  check (rule) (value) = verdict (vr-check rule value)

Section: The simple rules

  test-required : Text =
    "required: empty=" & check VrRequired "" & " filled=" & check VrRequired "x"

  test-min-length : Text =
    "min3: short=" & check (VrMinLength 3) "ab" & " exact=" & check (VrMinLength 3) "abc"

  test-max-length : Text =
    "max3: fits=" & check (VrMaxLength 3) "abc" & " over=" & check (VrMaxLength 3) "abcd"

Section: The character classes

  test-numeric : Text =
    "numeric: digits=" & check (VrPattern "number") "123"
    & " letters=" & check (VrPattern "number") "abc"
    & " mixed=" & check (VrPattern "number") "12a"

  test-alpha : Text =
    "alpha: lower=" & check (VrPattern "alpha") "abc"
    & " upper=" & check (VrPattern "alpha") "ABC"
    & " digits=" & check (VrPattern "alpha") "123"

 A letter is a letter in any script, so `alpha` takes these. The three
 groups are chosen to exercise three different paths, not to be decorative:
 the accented and Cyrillic forms are TIER 0, one byte each, and were what a
 band ending at 64 refused; the Greek is TIER 1, two bytes, and is refused
 by anything that decides a character on its lead byte.

 Punctuation is the control. CCE puts it at 65..96, BETWEEN the ASCII
 letters and the accented ones, so a letter test written as one widened
 range would accept it. This line is what fails if anyone ever closes that
 hole by widening rather than by asking.

  test-alpha-scripts : Text =
    "alpha-scripts: accented=" & check (VrPattern "alpha") "café"
    & " cyrillic=" & check (VrPattern "alpha") "дом"
    & " greek=" & check (VrPattern "alpha") "αβγ"
    & " punct=" & check (VrPattern "alpha") "a.b"

  test-numeric-wide : Text =
    "numeric-wide: greek=" & check (VrPattern "number") "α"
    & " digits=" & check (VrPattern "number") "42"

  test-email : Text =
    "email: with-at=" & check (VrPattern "email") "a@b"
    & " without=" & check (VrPattern "email") "ab"

  test-range : Text =
    "range 1..10: inside=" & check (VrRange 1 10) "5"
    & " below=" & check (VrRange 1 10) "0"
    & " above=" & check (VrRange 1 10) "99"

Section: An unknown pattern and a custom rule are permissive by design

  test-permissive : Text =
    "unknown-pattern=" & check (VrPattern "zzz") "anything" & " custom=" & check (VrCustom "c") "anything"

Section: The form

  form-two : FormValidation
  form-two = form-validation [field-validation "a" [VrRequired], field-validation "b" [VrMinLength 3]]

  test-form : Text =
    let f = validate-form form-two ["set", "xx"]
    in "form: valid=" & (if form-is-valid f then "true" else "false") & " count=" & show (f.form-field-count)

  test-error-hidden : Text =
    let f = validate-form form-two ["set", "xx"]
    in "untouched-error=[" & form-field-error f "b" & "]"

  test-error-shown : Text =
    let f = validate-form form-two ["set", "xx"]
    in let t = form-touch-field f "b"
    in "touched-error=[" & form-field-error t "b" & "]"

Section: Formatting

  test-format : Text =
    let f = validate-form form-two ["set", "xx"]
    in "format=[" & format-form-validation f & "]"

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni test-required
    print-line-uni test-min-length
    print-line-uni test-max-length
    print-line-uni test-numeric
    print-line-uni test-alpha
    print-line-uni test-alpha-scripts
    print-line-uni test-numeric-wide
    print-line-uni test-email
    print-line-uni test-range
    print-line-uni test-permissive
    print-line-uni test-form
    print-line-uni test-error-hidden
    print-line-uni test-error-shown
    print-line-uni test-format
  end
